<h1>Commands Reference</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Command behavior varies. Read the boundary as carefully as the feature.</p>

<table class="cmd-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Main limitation</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>scan</code></td><td>Match supported dependency coordinates to OSV advisories</td><td>Advisory data can lag and does not establish exploitability</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>analyze</code></td><td>Collect npm/PyPI heuristic registry and source-pattern evidence</td><td>Conditional and bounded; <code>--deep</code> remains incomplete</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>fix</code></td><td>Generate npm candidates cross-checked against OSV and registry data</td><td>Not compatibility or future-safety verification</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>guard</code></td><td>Assess an explicit public-npm install request before applying it</td><td>Narrow npm grammar; metadata-bound; scripts stay disabled</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>monitor</code></td><td>CI annotations/SARIF or early watch mode</td><td>Network and input gaps remain incomplete</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>explain</code></td><td>Ask a configured model to prioritize a valid completed scan</td><td>Opt-in model draft; not deterministic evidence</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>inspect</code></td><td>Collect evidence for one npm/PyPI coordinate</td><td>Does not determine whether a package is safe</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>doctor</code></td><td>Check runtime, parser fixtures, cache, and optional isolation support</td><td>A smoke test, not an audit</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>licenses</code></td><td>Inventory declared dependency licenses</td><td>Uses metadata, can be incomplete, and is not legal advice</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Common flags</h2>
<div class="code-block"><span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">vexes scan --path ./project --ecosystem npm --severity high</span>
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">vexes scan --json</span>
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">vexes scan --format sarif</span>
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">vexes scan --no-user-config --no-project-config</span></div>
<p><code>--no-project-config</code> prevents an inspected checkout from choosing ecosystems, ignores, severity, or signal suppression. Add <code>--no-user-config</code> for results independent of trusted runner-account policy.</p>

<h2><code>scan</code></h2>
<p>Use ecosystem values <code>npm</code>, <code>pypi</code>, <code>cargo</code>, <code>go</code>, <code>ruby</code>, <code>php</code>, <code>nuget</code>, <code>java</code>, <code>hex</code>, or <code>pub</code>. <code>--fix</code> on scan shows advisory-derived hints. Direct-import evidence never suppresses an advisory; the older <code>--min-reachability</code> option is accepted, warned, and ignored.</p>

<h2><code>analyze</code> and <code>inspect</code></h2>
<div class="code-block"><span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">vexes analyze --deep --json</span>
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">vexes analyze --explain express</span>
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">vexes inspect npm:express@4.21.2</span></div>
<p><code>--strict</code> exits 1 for surviving, non-ignored results at the active severity policy. Analyze emits text or JSON, not SARIF. Experimental <code>--sandbox</code> telemetry is Linux <code>bwrap</code>-only, npm-only, partial, and remains incomplete even after a launch.</p>

<h2><code>fix</code></h2>
<p>For npm, vexes selects a candidate that clears the advisory thresholds it saw, asks OSV about that exact candidate, confirms registry presence, and prints a quoted command. A no-match response is only a point-in-time lookup. Generate the lockfile, rescan it, and run your tests.</p>

<h2><code>guard</code></h2>
<div class="code-block"><span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">vexes guard -- npm install package-name</span></div>
<p><code>--setup</code> is intentionally disabled. <code>--force</code> can override HIGH heuristic evidence only; known advisories, CRITICAL evidence, and incomplete analysis remain blocking. JSON mode assesses without installing.</p>

<h2><code>explain</code></h2>
<p>Configure one of: <code>VEXES_AI_BASE</code> for an OpenAI-compatible endpoint; <code>ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL</code> plus authentication for an Anthropic-compatible endpoint; or <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> for hosted Anthropic. The command refuses malformed or incomplete scan envelopes and sends a bounded, sanitized finding summary—not package source—to the selected provider.</p>

<h2>Exit codes</h2>
<table class="cmd-table"><tbody>
  <tr><td><code>0</code></td><td>Requested supported checks complete, no finding at threshold; not a safety verdict</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>1</code></td><td>Finding meets policy</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code>2</code></td><td>Error or incomplete requested evidence</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
